upd-title = It tells you when to update.
upd-lede = Each release publishes a feed. Nestor reads it once a day, and the admin says what changed, what breaks and how to update. Satellites update from the admin.
upd-1 = One feed per release
upd-1-text = `releases.json`: every release, its changes by kind, and the satellite protocol versions it speaks. Nestor only reads it.
upd-2 = What breaks, said first
upd-2-text = Breaking changes come first in the notes, with the satellites the new release no longer speaks to.
upd-3 = The server, in one click
upd-3-text = Installed with uv or pip, Nestor installs the release into its own environment, checks it with `nestor check`, and goes back if it fails. With Docker, `docker compose pull`.
upd-4 = Two protocol versions at once
upd-4-text = The server accepts a set of protocol versions, so a release can keep the previous one while the satellites follow.
upd-satellite-title = A satellite fetches its own update.
upd-satellite-text = It looks for newer versions where it was installed from and reports them. When a person clicks, Nestor sends only that version, never a file or an address. The device installs it, and goes back if the new one does not connect within a minute.
upd-code-found = the satellite found a newer version at its own source
upd-code-asked = a person clicked Update in the admin
upd-code-installs = it installs it, then starts again on it
upd-docs = Updates
upd-protocol = The rules, in the protocol
upd-protocol-anchor = 10-updates
